# 🎪 Velvet & Fire — SRD
### Story Tools for the Romantic Circus Narrative Engine
*Created by Asa Nodelman (VelvetFireCircus)*

Welcome to the official Story Reference Document (SRD) for Velvet & Fire — Romantic Circus Adventure, a living-world interactive narrative built on craft intimacy, character agency, emotional stakes, and impressionistic heat.

This repository hosts the canonical Story Tools (STs) that power the narrative engine, define character behavior, regulate intimacy tone, and maintain continuity across chapters.

Everything here is intended for:
- Game initialization
- Chapter start-ups
- Continuity management
- External players running their own circus variations
- AI story engines referencing tools via raw links

## 📁 Story Tools Index

Each Story Tool is stored as its own Markdown file for clarity and modularity.

### ST-1 — Welcome to the Circus
`st-1-welcome-to-vf.md`
Defines the identity of Velvet & Fire as a game world: the living-circus model, the Heat Map, and the Endgame Cutscene structure.

### ST-2 — Emotional Engine
`st-2-emotional-engine.md`
Outlines emotional logic, consent systems, Heat progression, and NPC autonomy (the living characters principle).

### ST-3 — Vocabulary
`st-3-vocabulary.md`
Master list of craft, circus, intimacy, sensual, atmospheric, and character-specific vocabulary used across the narrative.

### ST-4 — Cast Story Tool
`st-4-cast.md`
Defines major and minor characters, their arcs, emotional structures, and long-term motives.

### ST-5 — Intimacy Protocol
`st-5-intimacy-protocol.md`
Ruleset for impressionistic intimacy, consent, pacing, tone, group dynamics, and escalation.

### ST-6 — Setting Story Tool
`st-6-setting.md`
Logistical, spatial, and environmental data for the circus: train layout, wagons, back yard, big top, town lots, daily rhythms.

### ST-7 — Narrative Voice & Engine Behavior
`st-7-narrative-voice-and-engine.md`
Defines how Velvet & Fire sounds: the narrator, point of view, tone rules, story structure, and the Engine/Player interface.

## 🧩 How to Use These Files

Story Tools are intended to be referenced by:
- Initialization Prompts
- Narrative engines
- Chapter scripts
- Game master frameworks
- Writers building modules or spin-off stories

Each ST includes:
- Definitions
- Constraints
- Behavioral rules
- Internal system logic

No tool contains prose. They are AI-to-AI documentation, dense and technical, designed for engine behavior.

## 🔗 Raw Links for External Access

Each Story Tool can be fetched using:

https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VelvetFireCircus/Velvet-and-Fire-SRD/refs/heads/main/<filename>

Perfect for Initialization Prompts and automated loading.

# ⭐ How to Initialize Architect Mode (Developer Use)

Architect Mode is the meta-workshop for Velvet & Fire — used to build and maintain the Story Tools, character engine, schedules, intimacy logic, and world systems.

To start Architect Mode in ChatGPT, you do not paste the full initializer anymore.  
You paste only the Loader Prompt below.

The loader fetches the real initialization instructions from:

    /ST-0/AMI.md

That file performs all Story Tool loading (ST-1 through ST-9), validation, behavior locking, and error handling.

────────────────────────────────────────────
Architect Mode Loader Prompt (paste into a fresh chat)
────────────────────────────────────────────

    BEGIN PROMPT — ARCHITECT MODE LOADER

    You are the AI host for **VELVET & FIRE — Architect Mode**, the development and design environment for the Velvet & Fire story engine.

    Architect Mode is a meta-workshop.  
    You do NOT run story scenes.  
    You do NOT simulate NPCs.  
    You do NOT enforce narrative or intimacy rules.  
    You focus entirely on structure, design, debugging, and system expansion.

    ────────────────────────────
    ST-0 — AMI BOOTSTRAP
    ────────────────────────────
    1. Fetch the following file from GitHub as raw text:

        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VelvetFireCircus/Velvet-and-Fire-SRD/main/ST-0/AMI.md

    2. Treat the content of AMI.md as your authoritative initialization instructions for this chat.
    3. Apply everything in AMI.md as if it had been pasted directly into this prompt.
    4. If AMI.md fails to load for any reason:
         • Stop initialization.  
         • Inform the user that ST-0/AMI.md could not be loaded and why.  
         • Ask them to correct the URL or paste the text of AMI.md directly.

    Do not load any other Story Tools yet. Wait for the instructions inside AMI.md.

    END PROMPT

────────────────────────────────────────────
What Happens Next?
────────────────────────────────────────────

Once pasted into ChatGPT, the loader will:

• Retrieve /ST-0/AMI.md  
• Execute the Architect Mode Initializer  
• Load ST-1 through ST-9 in order  
• Apply all Architect Mode rules  
• Then respond with:

    Architect Mode initialized. What would you like to build?

At that moment, the system is fully active.

────────────────────────────────────────────
Why Use ST-0?
────────────────────────────────────────────

Centralizing the initializer gives you:

• Single-file updates — change startup logic without touching the loader  
• Version control — clear diffs and controlled evolution  
• Lightweight chats — no repeated huge blocks  
• Future extensibility — ST-0 can grow into a proper bootstrap system

## 🎟️ About Velvet & Fire

Velvet & Fire is a historically-inspired romantic circus adventure focusing on:
- Found-family bonds
- Craft intimacy
- Real emotional stakes
- Living-world simulation
- Impressionistic sensuality
- Character agency
- Performative ritual
- Romance braided with danger

This SRD is the backbone of the entire circus world.

